                    <p>Azo Pigment Yellow Pigment (often classified under various subtypes such as Pigment Yellow 191 or others, depending on formulation) is a high-performance, organic pigment known for its bright, clean yellow shade, excellent lightfastness, and superior weather resistance. Part of the phthalocyanine pigment family, it is synthesized using copper phthalocyanine base structures that offer outstanding durability and consistent performance in a wide range of applications.</p>
                    <p>Available in different crystal modifications, it provides excellent color strength, transparency, and dispersibility making it an ideal choice for industrial and consumer applications where vibrant, long-lasting color is essential.</p>
